# AWS CCP — Compute

Which service provides resizable virtual servers in the cloud?
---
EC2
= Amazon EC2
= Elastic Compute Cloud
---
The original AWS compute service. You pick the instance type, AMI, and network.

What does AMI stand for?
---
Amazon Machine Image
= machine image
---
The template (OS plus installed software) an instance launches from.

Which service runs your code in response to events with no servers to manage?
---
Lambda
= AWS Lambda
---
Pay per request and per millisecond. A single invocation can run at most 15 minutes.

Which service is AWS's own container orchestrator?
---
ECS
= Amazon ECS
= Elastic Container Service
---
The AWS-native way to run Docker containers. EKS is the Kubernetes alternative.

Which service runs managed Kubernetes clusters?
---
EKS
= Amazon EKS
= Elastic Kubernetes Service
---
For teams already invested in Kubernetes. ECS is simpler if you are not.

Which serverless engine runs containers without any EC2 instances to manage?
---
Fargate
= AWS Fargate
---
A launch type for both ECS and EKS. You size the task, AWS finds the compute.

Which service stores and distributes your container images?
---
ECR
= Amazon ECR
= Elastic Container Registry
---
The AWS-hosted alternative to Docker Hub, wired into ECS and EKS permissions.

Which service takes just your application code and handles provisioning, load balancing, and scaling for you?
---
Elastic Beanstalk
= AWS Elastic Beanstalk
= Beanstalk
---
The AWS PaaS answer. You still keep full access to the EC2 instances underneath.

Which service offers simple virtual private servers with predictable monthly pricing?
---
Lightsail
= Amazon Lightsail
---
Bundled compute, storage, and networking. The easy on-ramp for small sites and blogs.

An EC2 {{Auto Scaling}} group adds or removes instances automatically to match demand.
---
Scale on a schedule, on metrics, or to maintain a fixed healthy count.

Which service distributes incoming traffic across multiple targets such as EC2 instances?
---
ELB
= Elastic Load Balancing
= Elastic Load Balancer
= load balancer
---
Pairs with Auto Scaling: one spreads the traffic, the other sizes the fleet.

Which load balancer type routes HTTP and HTTPS requests with path-based rules?
---
Application Load Balancer
~ Network Load Balancer
~ Gateway Load Balancer
~ Classic Load Balancer
---
Layer 7. Network Load Balancer is layer 4 for TCP at extreme throughput.

Which service runs AWS infrastructure and services inside your own data center?
---
Outposts
= AWS Outposts
---
A rack AWS delivers and manages on your premises. The heavyweight hybrid option.

Which service plans, schedules, and runs very large numbers of batch computing jobs?
---
Batch
= AWS Batch
---
It provisions the compute (including Spot) for you. Not to be confused with Lambda's 15-minute jobs.
